\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S(f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,k,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S(f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,k,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional}\\vdash\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S(f,V,k)\\leftrightarrow\\exists +_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k\\;\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S(f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional}\\vdash\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S(f,V,k)\\leftrightarrow\\exists +_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k\\;\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S(f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}algebraic\\text{-}dual}\\vdash V_k^\\vee\\coloneqq\\{f\\in k^V:\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S(f,V,k)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}algebraic\\text{-}dual}\\vdash V_k^\\vee\\coloneqq\\{f\\in k^V:\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S(f,V,k)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Linear functional: linear map to scalar field</li>\n<li>The data predicate retains the addition and scalar actions required by the exact upstream linear-map predicate; the three-place predicate is its existential projection.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_k^\\vee\">\\(V_k^\\vee\\)</span> is the algebraic dual. It is not the normed-space dual of bounded linear functionals.</li>\n<li>Riesz representation: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x^* \\leftrightarrow \\langle x^*, \\cdot \\rangle\">\\(x^* \\leftrightarrow \\langle x^*, \\cdot \\rangle\\)</span></li>\n<li>Hahn-Banach: extend bounded linear functionals</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Rudin, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Conway, A Course in Functional Analysis</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (fully explicit linear-map predicate, see [[../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S:V^7\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LinearFunctional}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\mathrm{LinearFunctionalData}_S(f,V,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+_k,\\cdot_k)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,k,k,+_V,\\odot_V,+